{"id":"bastard","name":"Bastard","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:bastard"],"types":[],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":["Instances Of"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Bastard","text":"In the Old Testament the rendering of the Hebrew word mamzer’, which means “polluted.” In Deut. 23:2, it occurs in the ordinary sense of illegitimate offspring. In Zech. 9:6, the word is used in the sense of foreigner. From the history of Jephthah we learn that there were bastard offspring among the Jews (Judg. 11:1-7). In Heb. 12:8, the word (Gr. nothoi) is used in its ordinary sense, and denotes those who do not share the privileges of God’s children."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","xlit":"ʼishshâh","gloss":"a woman","kjv":"ess, each, every, female","count":5,"share":0.38},{"strong":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","xlit":"yâlad","gloss":"to bear young","kjv":"bear, beget, birth, born","count":3,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H7971","lemma":"שָׁלַח","xlit":"shâlach","gloss":"to send away, for, or out","kjv":"any wise, appoint, bring, cast","count":3,"share":0.23}],"verses":["Gen.16.3","Judg.11.1","2Sam.11.2","2Sam.11.3","2Sam.11.5","Gen.16.15","Gen.19.36","Gen.19.37","Deut.23.2","2Sam.11.4","Zech.9.6","Gal.4.22","Heb.12.8"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"bath-sheba-bathsheba","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.091,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"uriah","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.091,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"instability","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.042,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"lasciviousness","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.029,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"chastity","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.025,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"adultery","type":"cooccur","shared":7,"jaccard":0.02,"w